if you've seen beetlejuice about  167 times then once you finish this  video you're going to want to see it  168th time keep watching so it'll be  even funnier the next time you see it  while beetlejuice is all about ghosts  monsters death and other objectively  spooky stuff it's actually not all that  scary this is thanks to michael keaton's  delightfully hammy work and the non-stop  bits of comedy to keep things from  tipping into full bore horror as it  turns out all that stuff happened during  rewrites and filming in its earliest  conceptions beetlejuice was a very  different movie in michael mcdowell's  script the maitland's death scene is  quite graphic and traumatic after that  they enlist the help of beetlejuice who  isn't so much an edgy clown in stripes  as he is an evil demon with wings while  he attempts to simply scare away the new  residents of the maitland's old house in  the movie he pretty much tries to kill  them in the original draft his  relationship with lydia dietz is  especially predatory as the ghost tries  to get with her in a way that's even  more inappropriate than the final film  before he tears her apart portraying  beetlejuice was a surprising departure  from michael keaton a star who was at  that point previously known for his  regular guy roles in comedies like  gung-ho and mr mom his performance here  showed he was more than capable of  pulling off horror gonzo comedy and well  just about anything to reinforce that  immediately after beetlejuice director  tim burton cast him as bruce wayne in  batman you're welcome with a  professional here  burton is a quirky filmmaker who often  makes off-the-wall casting decisions  while keaton might have been a somewhat  surprising choice he actually wasn't  even burton's first pick for the title  role he initially wanted beloved actor  crooner candyman and all-around  entertainer sammy davis jr for the part  up to that point the script called for  the character to be a bit more evil with  a las vegas lounge singer kind of vibe  since davis was a former rat packer he  fit the bill in that last regard credit  for keaton's casting goes to producer  david geffen who talked burton out of  his pick and suggested he'd check out  the future dark knight instead you like  it  during burton and keaton's first meeting  the former tried his best to explain  beetlejuice's far out concept to his  eventual star and apparently he didn't  do such a great job of communicating his  admittedly outlandish ideas in a  conversation with charlie rose in 2014  keaton said i didn't understand what he  was talking about but i liked him i went  oh well this guy's something i said i i  wish i could do it you seem like a  really nice guy and i know you're  creative but i don't know what you're i  don't get it burton was able to convince  keaton to meet again and that time he  went into more detail about the project  the actors still didn't understand and  politely declined beetlejuice once more  undeterred burton persuaded him to take  a third meeting and this time he rattled  off some ideas that keaton said just  logged in his brain he asked burton for  some time to think it over which he  spent building the characters so he  could wrap his mind around it say it  once saying twice third time's a charm  keaton called up some associates at the  production studio's wardrobe house and  asked for various clothing choices from  different time periods he also requested  some help in creating the character's  appearance he wanted his hair to look  like he was shocked by an electrical  outlet in his face to have mold on it  all that stuff wound up in the  character's final design  tim burton wanted to call the movie  beetlejuice but he had to put up a bit  of a fight to make it happen as a young  filmmaker at the time burton had to deal  with a certain amount of studio  interference and executives initially  planned to give the movie the bland and  forgettable title house ghosts  he hated that idea so he tried to play a  little game with his bosses he suggested  the title scared sheetless instead  thinking the powers that be would relent  and let him go for beetlejuice but the  plan backfired the studio actually liked  scared sheetless and seriously  considered releasing the movie under  that title ultimately burton got his way  after threatening to hurl himself out a  window over 30 years later the role of  awkward teenage goth lydia dietz still  ranks among winona ryder's most  definitive and popular performances  beetlejuice launched a young actor into  mega stardom and marked her first  collaboration with tim burton with whom  she'd work again on edward scissorhands  and frankenweenie looking back it's hard  to believe that ryder just barely landed  the part and only landed it after  beating out an actor who doesn't seem  very burtonesque at all who's the boss  teen sensation alyssa milano i myself am  strange and unusual  in a 2016 interview with huff post live  milano revealed that casting for the  part of lydia came down to two choices  ryder and herself when reflecting on how  badly she wanted the part she said you  always wonder what would have happened  differently in my life had that worked  out not that i would want it to be any  different but it's just an interesting  thought game  burton helped kathryn o'hara's career  with beetlejuice and the movie had a  major effect on her off-screen life too  brooding mysterious odd these are words  one would use to describe tim burton but  probably not romantic or matchmaker  still according to o'hara he exercised  that part of his personality on the set  of beetlejuice bo welch served as the  movie set designer so he was very much  responsible for giving the film its  sensational and original postmodern  horror look and burton thought that he  and o'hara would make a very cute couple  so he tried to make it happen o'hara  told digital spy that tim actually set  us up to date if you don't let me gut  out this house and make it my own i will  go and stay and i will take you with me  they hit it off and a couple of years  later welch and o'hara got married and  had two children those kids owe their  lives to a casting switcheroo their  parents may never have met if o'hara  hadn't replaced angelica houston who won  the role of delia but had to drop out of  the project after she fell ill  one unexpected ripple effect of  beetlejuice it made calypso cool again  which hadn't been in the pop  consciousness much since harry belafonte  topped the charts in the 1950s and early  60s i didn't even know i could do the  calypso during a dinner party new  haunted house residents delia and  charles dietz and their guests become  compelled by ghostly forces to perform a  musical number set to deo that's just  one of multiple belafonte songs in the  movie in the opening minutes alec  baldwin's adam maitland listens to  sweetheart from venenzuela later lydia  joyfully dances and floats to jump in  the line shake senora and deo also plays  earlier in the film when gina davis's  barbara maitland peruses the handbook of  the recently deceased while adam works  on his model none of that appeared in  the first version of michael mcdowell's  screenplay when writer warren skarin  took a pass his draft included classic r  b the haunted dinner party scene  involved the humans dancing to the ink  spots if i didn't care and suggested  that lydia would provide a rendition of  when a man loves a woman where did the  calypso come from catherine o'hara  according to her on-screen husband  jeffrey jones o'hara suggested that the  musical forum would liven up the dinner  party scene tim burton and the rest of  the filmmaking team dug the idea so they  set about getting the rights to old  calypso tunes and threading them  throughout the movie  he's gone on to log numerous hits and  cult classics but beetlejuice might be  tim burton's signature movie all his  calling cards are present a ghoulish  protagonist a mixture of high comedy and  spooky darkness and quaint puppet and  model-based special effects in  beetlejuice our title character attempts  to terrify the deet's family out of the  former maitland home by rising up out of  a town model michael keaton appears  ghostly white mouth the gape and wearing  a mobile on his head that's comprised of  little dragons and hideous sea monsters  this mobile comes in the form of a black  and white striped tube hat to match his  primary costume and the top of the  umbrella-like contraption is overseen by  a little model of some kind of undead  creature that creature is a dead ringer  for jack skellington the main character  in burton's a nightmare before christmas  which wasn't released until five years  after beetlejuice  given how popular it remains the absence  of a sequel to beetlejuice is surprising  but it isn't for a lack of effort  shortly after the first film burton  created an outline that writer jonathan  jims turned into a script titled  beetlejuice goes hawaiian as jim's told  fangoria tim thought it would be funny  to match the surfing backdrop of a beach  movie with some sort of german  expressionism because they're totally  wrong together beetlejuice goes hawaiian  was publicly announced in 1990 with  michael keaton winona ryder catherine  o'hara and jeffrey jones all agreeing to  reprise their roles the story found the  characters heading to hawaii to check up  on diet's construction project a casino  built on top of a sacred hawaiian burial  ground along the way lydia visits the  worlds of the undead and beetlejuice  wins a surfing contest but then warner  brothers offered burton total creative  control on batman returns so he and  keaton went off to do that interest died  the actors moved on and the script was  never filmed nor was a subsequent effort  by beetlejuice co-writer warren skarin  called beetlejuice in love in which the  ghost with the most offers up his  services to some new characters in 2011  warner brothers decided to explore a  sequel once more with a script  potentially written by pride and  prejudice and zombies author seth graham  smith that never turned into cinematic  gold either however the beetlejuice  sequel has yet to find itself in the  lost souls rule efforts to bring a  second film to life continued and in  february of 2022 plan b a production  company founded by brad pitt jennifer  aniston and brad gray became involved  will beetlejuice 2 finally be  resurrected  only time will tell check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about your favorite movies  are coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]

